M5Stack firmware archive

The sketches come from M5Stack Arduino documentation at revision
6ee4f2fb9dca1c671e475407cb709109a699cf1a. Each firmware.json identifies
the English page, source section and any linked library example.
Copyright and applicable terms remain with the respective rightsholders.
The M5Unified WAV sketch uses the documented Cardputer-Adv chip select
and the generated SD audio fixture. The LTR5XX manifest pins the original
documentation download and its checksum.

M5Unified and M5GFX are MIT licensed. Their notices are under licenses/.
The manifests identify the versions of M5Cardputer, M5Unit-Sonic and
Arduino-IRremote where used. Arduino-ESP32 contains LGPL code and
components under separate licenses, including Apache-2.0 ESP-IDF code.
https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32
https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf

The Arduino ELF and BIN files described in the manifests are build outputs
of those sketches and components. Exact originals are kept locally.
The public archive contains their hashes and flash layouts.

UIFlow2 v2.5.3 is an official M5Stack release artifact. Its original bytes
are available from M5Burner via the URL in the manifest.

The CoreS3 replay runner adapts the pinned esp32sim runner. Its MIT notice
is under licenses/. The SD media, camera patterns and input tones were
generated for virtual-device validation.
